{"url": "https://www.monash.edu/science/schools/biological-sciences", "final_url": "https://www.monash.edu/science/schools/biological-sciences", "status": 200, "method": "chromium", "fetched": "2026-10-31", "text": "Home\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nPrevious menu\nToggle navigation\nSCIENCE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nSkip to content\nSkip to navigation\nHome\nMonash Australia\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nMonash Australia\nMonash India\nMonash Indonesia\nMonash Malaysia\nMonash Prato\nMonash Suzhou\nMonash Boston Hub\nCourses\nMonash Online\nLibrary\nDonate\nSTAFF\nStaff\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTAFF\nStaff portal\nIntranet\nM-Space\nThe Insider\nSTUDENTS\nStudents\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nSTUDENTS\nStudent portal\nStudent website\nMonash Connect\nMonash Online hub\nALUMNI\nAlumni\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nALUMNI\nAlumni portal\nAlumni website\nSEARCH\nSCIENCE\nABOUT US\nFUTURE STUDENTS\nCURRENT STUDENTS\nRESEARCH\nMORE\nAPPLY TO STUDY\nSchool of Biological Sciences\nPrevious\nBIOLOGICAL SCIENCES\nMeeting the grand challenges of our era through education and research.\nDR LESLEY ALTON\nCuriosity drives science and maths underpins every discipline\nFind out more\nNext\n12\nSchool of Biological Sciences\nUse your curious and creative mind to analyse and interpret data. Discover the hows and whys of our world.\nCURRENT STUDENTS\nGet your coursework info\nCHOOSE YOUR MAJOR\n.\nFUTURE STUDENTS\nGet set for a future in biological sciences\nEXPLORE YOUR OPTIONS\n.\nHonours\nGenetics/genomics, ecology, evolution, plant sciences and zoology. Use your love of biology to make the world a better place. Current Honours Projects\nMaster Degrees\nCreate the future you want to live in.\nMaster of Environment and Sustainability\nMaster of Genome Analytics\nPostgraduate\nWhether you think global or local, a PhD helps you make an impact on your community.\nResearch\nWe have research strengths in three broad discipline areas:\nEcology and Conservation\nEvolution in a Changing World\nGenetics, Genomics, and Health\nResearch Centres and Special Initiatives\nTeaching\nWe are dedicated to excellence in teaching and providing a first class, international education to students from all around the world.\nQuick Links\nLeadership Team\nContact Us\nOur People\nEquity, Diversity and Inclusion\nMental Health and Wellbeing\nDisability Services\nOur Seminars\nOur Facilities\nSchool Intranet (restricted access)\nNews and Stories\nFind us on Twitter\nLatest news from The School of Biological Sciences\nProtecting isn't enough: New research reveals the missing link is creating integrated conservation landscapes\nNew Monash University research has revealed how countries could dramatically strengthen their conservation networks by looking beyond the boundaries of national parks and protected areas \u2013 and focusing on how these areas connect.\nBIOLOGY\nInvasive ragweed is rewriting its genome as it conquers new territory\nAn invasive weed responsible for severe pollen allergies around the world has revealed how rapidly plant genomes can change as species colonise new environments.\nBIOLOGICAL SCIENCES\nProtecting Australia\u2019s native bees from global pollinator decline requires urgent action\nAustralia is home to an extraordinary diversity of native bees, but scientists warn that major gaps in our knowledge mean species could be declining before we have the data to recognise what is happening.\nBIOLOGICAL SCIENCES\nHotter temperatures cause hidden cellular ageing in wild birds\nMonash research in Proceedings of the Royal Society B shows sublethal heat accelerates telomere damage in purple-crowned fairy-wrens during key life stages. Dense vegetation buffers this cellular decay, highlighting habitat preservation as critical.\nBIOLOGICAL SCIENCES\nProfessor Craig White appointed Vice-Provost\nProfessor Craig White has been appointed Vice-Provost of Monash University, starting Monday 12 October. A distinguished evolutionary physiologist, he previously served as Head of Biological Sciences, where Professor Anne Peters will step in as\nGENERAL NEWS\nView more articles\nWe acknowledge and pay respects to the Elders and Traditional Owners of the land on which our Australian campuses stand. Information for Indigenous Australians\nCOMMUNITY\nFaculties\nLocations\nDiversity and inclusion\nSafety and security\nSustainability\nRESOURCES\nImportant dates\nHow to apply\nA-Z index\nPolicy Bank\nFAQs\nCONTACT\nContact us\nCampus maps\nJobs at Monash\nRecruit a student\nPay online\nNEWS\nLatest news\nMonash Lens\nPodcasts\nA Different Lens\nMonash Life\nON OUR SITE\nCurrent students\nStaff intranet\nSite map\nREGISTERED AUSTRALIAN UNIVERSITY\nABN: 12 377 614 012\nTEQSA Provider ID: PRV12140\nCRICOS PROVIDER NUMBER\nMonash University: 00008C\nMonash College: 01857J\nAUTHORISED BY\nExecutive Director, Marketing\nWebsite feedback\nLast updated: Feb 2026\nAccessibility\nDisclaimer & copyright\nTerms & conditions\nData privacy & cyber security\nData Consent Settings\nCopyright \u00a9 2026 Monash University\nWe use cookies to improve your experience, but you can choose which ones we use, and opt-out at any time. You can find more information in our Website Terms and Conditions\nAccept all\nCookie settings", "links": [["Home", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["Courses", "https://www.monash.edu/study/courses"], ["Monash Online", "https://online.monash.edu/"], ["Library", "https://www.monash.edu/library"], ["Donate", "https://www.monash.edu/giving"], ["Science", "https://www.monash.edu/science"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["About us", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about"], ["Schools in Science", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about/schools"], ["Women in Science", "https://www.monash.edu/science/about/women-in-science"], ["Women in Science", "https://www.m